cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Temari in academic work, please cite this repository. If you publish ionization cross sections obtained through it, please also cite the two Bote-Salvat papers listed under references."
type: software
title: "Temari"
abstract: "Atomic scattering and excitation factors from first principles. Temari solves an isolated atom from scratch - self-consistent field, bound orbitals, distorted continuum waves - and derives the scattering and excitation factors needed by electron microscopy, spectroscopy and transport simulation. No external atomic-structure code, no fitted parameter tables, no dependencies beyond the Julia standard library."
authors:
  - family-names: "Seto"
    given-names: "Yusuke"
    affiliation: "Osaka Metropolitan University, Japan"
url: "https://seto77.github.io/Temari/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/seto77/Temari"
license: MIT
version: "0.9.0"
date-released: "2026-08-05"
keywords:
  - atomic physics
  - electron microscopy
  - ionization form factor
  - inner-shell ionization
  - STEM-EDX
  - EELS
  - generalized oscillator strength
  - Dirac-Hartree-Fock-Slater
  - distorted wave
  - Julia

